--- body ---
## Context
Roar steps 7, 8, the step-9 preflight and step 10 are deterministic, but the
skill holds them as bash blocks the model retypes and runs turn by turn, each
turn re-reading the full cached session context. Transcript count on padme
(2026-10-11, 400 most recent sessions, 75 roars, whole-roar measure): median
16 turns starting at 215k context, ~420k cache-read input equivalents per roar;
29 roars start above 256k (~750k each). Collapsing the mechanical steps into one
command saves an estimated ~40% per median roar (derived: assumes 8-10 of 16
turns are mechanical, not measured per step). Preferred over a phase-B subagent
(journal 2026-10-11-roar-clear-verdict-survey): no handoff, helps small roars too.

## Exit criteria
- [x] One script under `skills/roar/` runs ticket close, `check-close-claims.sh`, tracker-sibling detection (reports "integration review due", does not perform it), step-9 preflight and explicitly scoped branch cleanup; ends with a one-screen report
- [x] Cleanup accepts only explicitly supplied source branches and full approved head OIDs from the current task's actually merged PRs; repeatable local/remote targets support multi-PR tasks; no targets deletes nothing; unrelated merged branches remain
- [x] Exact refs/OIDs and integration ancestry are checked; default/current/symbolic/occupied branches remain; unreadable evidence fails closed; drift refuses before deletion; ordinary local `-d` merge/worktree refusal and remote OID lease remain; no delete-and-restore or human-output parsing
- [x] Behavioral tests cover scoped cleanup, foreign merged refs, default/current/worktree protection, changed local/remote tips, self-tracking unmerged tips, idempotence and custom remote fetch scope
- [x] Exit codes distinguish clean / findings / could-not-look; no all-clear on unreadable forge or cleanup evidence
- [x] `skills/roar/SKILL.md` states caller ownership/evidence obligations and delegates mechanical phases; helper never removes worktrees; `rules/git.md` delegates only current-task cleanup, leaving repository-wide housekeeping to lair/molt
- [ ] Remeasure turns per roar on roars run after the merge and record the result in the journal — discharged by follow-up 1090, not met at merge
